      "jcr:created": "Fri Oct 10 2025 20:21:59 GMT+0000",
      "text": "<p><i><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">1-minute read</span></i></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Henry Ford Health, a Michigan-based hospital system with 13 locations and 50,000 staff members, is expanding its virtual care model enterprise-wide following a successful virtual nursing pilot in collaboration with care.ai, now part of Stryker. In the initial pilot, virtual nurses supported bedside teams by managing admissions, rounding and discharge tasks, without reducing the number of bedside staff.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><b>Working together to improve care delivery</b></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Every health system has unique needs, making partnership essential for successful virtual care deployment. To meet Henry Ford Health’s specific requirements, care.ai partnered with SONIFI Health’s interactive platform to create a customized solution focused on seamless integration and workflow alignment.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">This case study highlights how virtual care is helping Henry Ford Health achieve its goals of:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Creating cost savings and safety improvements</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Improving patient outcomes and care quality</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Increasing HCAHPS and patient satisfaction scores</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Oct 14 2025 19:37:11 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true"
    },
